WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.088
In the autumn of 976, the Kaifeng palace was bathed in moonlight, silent and still.

00:00:08.438 --> 00:00:15.710
In the imperial study, candlelight flickered gently, casting long shadows on the wall.

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:23.332
Emperor Taizu of Song, Zhao Kuangyin, sat with his younger brother Zhao Guangyi by the candlelight, drinking tea and chatting.

00:00:23.682 --> 00:00:29.730
That night, there were only swaying candle shadows and the soft sound of an axe handle.

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:38.000
The next morning, white banners hung in the palace, and the officials, in white mourning clothes, bowed their heads in grief.

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:43.438
People only knew that Emperor Taizu had died in the night.

00:00:43.788 --> 00:00:50.220
Zhao Guangyi inherited the throne as Emperor Taizong of Song, and the officials paid homage to the new ruler.

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:52.850
What exactly happened that night?

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:59.728
The legend of 'candle shadows and the sound of an axe' remains an unsolved historical mystery to this day.

